@database "context_summarizer"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: context_summarizer.guide 1.0 (29.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Context Summarizer"
@{h1}Context Summarizer

A long conversation gets expensive and at some point no longer fits the
model. The Context Summarizer shrinks it: before an LLM call it has a
second, cheaper model summarize the older messages and puts the summaries
in their place. The prompts and the most recent messages stay as they
were. It runs by itself when a conversation grows past a number of
messages or a share of the model's context window; an agent can also
start it with a tool, and you with @{tt}/summarize@{utt}. The
@{b}Context Summarizer@{ub} panel lists every run with what it saved and
what it wrote.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Context Summarizer panel with the runs of a session"}

@{code}
For users
  @{"  The Context Summarizer panel  " link panel}

For agents and developers
  @{"  The summarize tool  " link summarize}
  @{"  The check_stats tool  " link check_stats}
  @{"  The summarizing hook  " link hook}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node panel "The Context Summarizer panel"
@{h1}The Context Summarizer panel

Open it from the launcher (@{b}Context & memory@{ub}, "Context
Summarizer"), or from a session's info button, which opens it on that
session.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Context Summarizer panel"}

@{h2}Which runs it shows

The panel follows the chat: it shows the runs of the session open there
and switches with it. Opened from a session's info button it stays on
that session -- the toolbar says so, and @{b}Follow the chat@{ub} lets go
of it. @{b}All sessions@{ub} shows the runs of every session, with a
column naming the session; that view is an admin's, anyone else gets
"The history could not be loaded" and the reason. With no session open
the panel says so and asks for nothing.

The list reloads every 5 seconds; the menu next to the reload button sets
another interval or turns it off.

@{h2}What you see

@{bullet}Four figures: the runs (and how many were applied, rejected and
skipped), the tokens saved, the messages summarized and the average
reduction. Tokens, messages and reduction count applied runs only.
@{bullet}The runs, newest first, the newest 100 -- a line above the table
says when there are more. Each row has the time, the outcome, the messages
before and after, the tokens before and after, the tokens saved and the
reduction. A click on a column head sorts by it.

What the outcomes mean:

@{table}
Outcome | Means
applied | the summaries replaced the older messages
rejected | the summaries were written but saved too little; the conversation stayed as it was
skipped | too few older messages, or too small ones to ever save enough; no summary was asked for
@{body}

A run that did not start at all -- the conversation below the thresholds,
or the pause after the last run not over -- is not listed.

@{h2}What you can do

@{bullet}A row -- click, Enter or Space -- opens the run in a drawer: its
figures, how many chunks were summarized and how many failed, the
summaries it wrote and the messages they replaced (each cut at 5000
characters). A rejected or skipped run kept no messages. A run that has
dropped out of the history meanwhile is refused with a notice.
@{bullet}The trash button forgets every run of every session, after
asking. Only an admin may (anyone, with authentication off); for anyone
else the server refuses and the panel shows why.

The runs are kept in the memory of the server process, at most the last
1000, and are gone after a restart. A run made by an agent in another
process (an @{tt}agent-cli@{utt} run) is not among them.
@endnode

@node summarize "The summarize tool"
@{h1}The summarize tool

@{tt}context_summarizer_summarize@{utt} (named after the plugin instance)
summarizes the conversation now, whatever its size. It is what
@{tt}/summarize [reason]@{utt} runs at the chat prompt. It runs the same
steps as the hook (see @{"  The summarizing hook  " link hook}) but skips
the size check and the pause between runs -- and it starts that pause
for the hook.

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
reason | free text, returned in the answer and logged; without it "manual_trigger"
chunk_size | 2 to 50: older messages summarized together; without it the configured summarization_chunk_size (10)
preserve_recent | 2 to 100: recent messages kept as they are; without it the configured preserve_recent_count (10)
@{body}

Both numbers hold for this run only; other runs, also running at the same
time, keep the configured values.

@{h2}Answers

@{bullet}@{tt}status: "success"@{utt} with @{tt}original_count@{utt} and
@{tt}summarized_count@{utt} (messages before and after, the prompts
counted), @{tt}tokens_saved@{utt} (an estimate), @{tt}summary_preview@{utt}
(the first 200 characters of the first summary), @{tt}reason@{utt} and
@{tt}modified@{utt}.
@{bullet}@{tt}modified: false@{utt}: nothing changed, and
@{tt}not_applied@{utt} says why -- @{tt}insufficient_old_messages@{utt}
(fewer than two messages older than the ones kept),
@{tt}insufficient_potential_reduction@{utt} (even dropping all older
messages would not save the minimum reduction),
@{tt}insufficient_reduction@{utt} (the summaries saved too little) or
@{tt}no_context_window@{utt} (the answering model's window is unknown).
@{bullet}An empty conversation answers @{tt}original_count: 0@{utt} and
"No messages in conversation".
@{bullet}@{tt}status: "error"@{utt} with @{tt}error@{utt}: a chunk_size or
preserve_recent out of range ("preserve_recent must be a whole number from
2 to 100, got 500"), a call without a session ("Session context not
available (session_id or agent missing)"), or a failed run
("Summarization failed: ..."). Nothing is changed then.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"reason": "planning is done", "preserve_recent": 20}
@{body}
@endnode

@node check_stats "The check_stats tool"
@{h1}The check_stats tool

@{tt}context_summarizer_check_stats@{utt} (no parameters) measures the
conversation, for an agent deciding whether to summarize. @{tt}/stats@{utt}
at the chat prompt runs it.

@{table}
Field | Means
message_count | messages, the prompts included
estimated_tokens | estimate of the messages plus the tool definitions
tool_definition_tokens | the tool definitions' share of it
actual_tokens | the prompt tokens of the session's last LLM call, from context_usage_tracker; 0 without one, or when a compaction since made it stale
total_tokens | the larger of the two
context_window | the window of the model answering the session
utilization_percentage | total_tokens as a share of the window
trigger_threshold | summarization_trigger_percentage, in percent
max_messages | the message count that triggers the hook for this agent; 0 when none does -- also when the hook is switched off for the agent
recommendation | "summarize" when the utilization reaches the threshold or the messages exceed max_messages, else "ok"
@{body}

An empty conversation answers zeros and "ok"; without a session the
answer is @{tt}{"status": "error", "error": "Session context not
available"}@{utt}.
@endnode

@node hook "The summarizing hook"
@{h1}The summarizing hook

@{tt}summarize_context@{utt} runs before every LLM call of every agent
while the plugin instance is enabled -- it is on by default -- after
context_engineer's hook.

@{h2}When it fires

Either condition is enough:

@{bullet}@{b}The message count@{ub}: more messages than
@{tt}max_messages@{utt}, the prompts counted. The shipped configuration
sets 200.
@{bullet}@{b}The tokens@{ub}: the larger of the session's last measured
prompt tokens (from context_usage_tracker, unless a compaction made them
stale) and an estimate of the messages plus the tool definitions reaches
@{tt}summarization_trigger_percentage@{utt} of the answering model's
context window. The shipped configuration sets 80%.

In practice it is the message count that fires it: tool-call chains
reach 200 messages long before 80% of a large window. For an agent that
also runs context_engineer's hook -- it is off by default and on for
@{tt}multi_turn_agent@{utt} and the agents built on it -- context_engineer
prunes at 190 messages first, and the summarizer steps in when that did
not bring the count under 200. For every other agent the summarizer is
the first to act.

It does nothing when the answering model's window is unknown, and nothing
for @{tt}min_time_between_summarizations@{utt} seconds (500 in the shipped
configuration) after a run of the same session that sent the summarizing
model at least one call -- applied, rejected or failed alike, and a manual
run too.

@{h2}What a run does

@{bullet}Tool calls without a result are removed from assistant messages
(not from the last message: its calls are still running).
@{bullet}The messages are split into the system messages (kept, when
@{tt}preserve_system_messages@{utt} is on), the last
@{tt}preserve_recent_count@{utt} messages (kept) and the older ones. A
tool result in the kept part whose call is older goes with its call.
@{bullet}The running turn's own messages from a person are never
summarized: every message a person wrote (or the wake of a woken run)
since the model's last final answer -- the task, and anything typed into
the run while it worked. An answer a hook followed up on (a "Continue"
note) does not end the turn, also when a person wrote into the run after
that note. An answer followed directly by a message from a person does
end it: the stored history cannot tell that message from the question
of a new turn. When a long tool chain has pushed them out of
the recent messages, each stays where it is, between the summaries of
what came before and after it.
@{bullet}Fewer than two older messages, or older messages too small to
reach @{tt}min_summary_reduction@{utt} even if they vanished: skipped.
@{bullet}The older messages are cut into chunks of
@{tt}summarization_chunk_size@{utt}, a call and its results always in
one chunk. More than @{tt}max_chunks@{utt} chunks, counted over all the parts
between those messages, make the chunks larger instead; only a turn with
more such parts than @{tt}max_chunks@{utt} goes past it, one chunk per
part. All chunks go to the summarizing model (@{tt}llm_profile@{utt})
at once, each with @{tt}summary_prompt_template@{utt}. A chunk of one
message, or one whose call fails, stays as it was.
@{bullet}If the new conversation is not at least
@{tt}min_summary_reduction@{utt} smaller (estimated), the run is
rejected and nothing changes. Otherwise it is applied.

The chat shows the run as a status line: "Summarizing 30 older messages
using LLM (preserving 10 recent messages)", then "Summarized 30 messages:
41200 -> 9800 tokens (76.2% reduction)" -- or "Not applied: 12.0%
reduction is below the 30.0% minimum". A skipped run shows no line.

@{h2}Switching it off, and max_messages per agent

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  hooks:
    overrides:
      context_summarizer.summarize_context:
        enabled: false        # this agent is never summarized
@{body}

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  hooks:
    overrides:
      context_summarizer.summarize_context:
        max_messages: 120     # this agent: after 120 messages
@{body}

@{tt}max_messages@{utt} is the only setting an agent's override changes;
every other setting comes from the plugin's server entry (see
@{"  Setting it up  " link setup}).
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The tools

The tool descriptions and parameter descriptions come from the plugin's
@{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}; the answers and error texts are those in
@{"  The summarize tool  " link summarize} and
@{"  The check_stats tool  " link check_stats}. The call's status line
ends with its result: "Summarized 32 → 14 messages (saved ~3711 tokens)",
"Not summarized: insufficient_old_messages", "Context: 48 messages,
~31000 tokens (incl. 2400 tool def tokens) (31.0% of 100000)".

@{h2}After a compaction

What the model keeps: its prompts, the system messages of the
conversation (moved to the front, before the summaries), the last
@{tt}preserve_recent_count@{utt} messages (10) and what a person wrote in
the running turn (the task, and anything typed into the run since),
exactly as they were.

What it loses: every other older message -- the text of the conversation, the
tool calls with their arguments and the full tool results. In their place
it gets one user message per chunk, marked as written by the plugin, not
by a person:

@{code}
[Summary of 10 older messages (chunk 1/3)]

The user asked for a deployment plan; we chose PostgreSQL and ...
@{body}

The chat shows these as injected messages of the plugin instance
(@{tt}context_summarizer@{utt}), not as something you wrote. /undo, /retry
and the turn counting of other plugins pass over them and find the turns
at the questions people wrote -- the running turn's are still there,
since they are never summarized; an earlier turn whose question went
into a summary is no longer a turn of its own.

The summarizing model reads each older message as "n. ROLE (time): text"
with its tool calls; images, audio and other non-text parts are not in
what it reads, so they are gone after the run. Reasoning carried over
from the model's earlier turns (encrypted reasoning, thought signatures)
across the replaced span is marked unusable. A manual run from inside a
tool call keeps that call: its result follows the summaries as usual.

@{h2}Tokens and cache

An applied run rewrites the conversation behind the prompts. The
provider's prompt cache keeps only the prompts in front; the next call
pays the rest of the (now much shorter) conversation in full once, and
from then on the history grows append-only again until the next run. The
summaries themselves cost one call of the summarizing model per chunk --
at most 10 per run by default (more only when a turn's messages from a
person split the older part into more pieces than that). The pause between automatic runs (500
seconds in the shipped setup) keeps a rejected run from repeating on
every step. After an applied run the session's measured token figures
are marked stale, so later hooks and check_stats go by the estimate until
the next LLM call measures again.

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}The summary is only as good as the summarizing model; a chunk it
fails on stays in full, and a run whose chunks all fail is rejected.
@{bullet}If the summarizing profile cannot be created at all (a typo in
@{tt}llm_profile@{utt}), the answering model summarizes instead. An
outage of the summarizing model at run time is not caught that way: the
chunks stay in full and the conversation does not shrink.
@{bullet}Tool results are summarized like any other text. A tool whose
result must survive word for word belongs in the recent messages or in a
store the agent can read again.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

The plugin is on in the default configuration (@{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}):

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    context_summarizer:
      type: context_summarizer
      enabled: true
      config:
        llm_profile: or-deepseek-flash
        max_message_preview_length: 5000
        min_time_between_summarizations: 500
        max_chunks: 10
        max_messages: 200
        summarization_trigger_percentage: 0.8
@{body}

With the instance enabled the hook runs for every agent. The tools only
for an agent whose allowlist names them:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  tools:
    allowed:
      - "+context_summarizer/*"
@{body}

@{h2}Server settings

These go under @{tt}config:@{utt} in the server entry; what is not set
there takes the default below.

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
max_messages | 0 | fire above this many messages; 0: by tokens only
summarization_trigger_percentage | 0.60 | fire when the tokens reach this share of the window
preserve_recent_count | 10 | recent messages kept as they are
preserve_system_messages | true | keep system messages; false: they are summarized like the others
summarization_chunk_size | 10 | older messages per summary
max_chunks | 10 | most summaries per run, the chunks grow instead; 0: no limit
llm_profile | turbo | the profile that writes the summaries
summary_prompt_template | see schema.yaml | the prompt; {messages} is replaced by the chunk; empty refuses to start
min_summary_reduction | 0.3 | how much smaller the conversation must get to be applied
min_time_between_summarizations | 200 | seconds between automatic runs of a session
max_tracked_sessions | 200 | sessions whose last run the pause remembers
max_message_preview_length | 5000 | characters of each message the panel keeps
@{body}

The summarizing client is created once per process, on the first run; a
changed @{tt}llm_profile@{utt} takes effect after a restart.

@{h2}Behind the panel

@{table}
Method | Path | Answer
GET | /plugins/context_summarizer/history?session_id=&limit= | the newest limit runs (1 to 1000, default 100) without their messages, and the figures over all of them
GET | /plugins/context_summarizer/events/{id} | one run with the messages it replaced and the summaries; 404 when gone
POST | /plugins/context_summarizer/clear | forgets every run
@{body}

A user sees the runs of her own sessions; another user's session answers
as one without runs, and its runs as gone. All sessions at once and
clearing are an admin's (403 otherwise).
@endnode
